        "original_id": "6dca6fc1-12f9-509a-b0c9-33f4713427f8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Carroll County, Ohio; Homewood Field; San Diego, California\n- People: Charles Carroll of Carrollton; Doc Watson\n- Topics: Declaration of Independence; Major League Baseball\n\nFacts:\n- Carroll County, Ohio, is named for Charles Carroll of Carrollton, the last surviving signer of the Declaration of Independence.\n- Charles Carroll of Carrollton was the only Catholic signatory of the Declaration of Independence.\n- Charles John \"Doc\" Watson was born in Carroll County, Ohio, on January 30, 1886.\n- Charles John \"Doc\" Watson was a pitcher in Major League Baseball.\n- Charles John \"Doc\" Watson died in San Diego, California, on December 30, 1949.\n- Homewood Field takes its name, like the entire campus, from the estate name of Charles Carroll of Carrollton.",
